          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">a universe waiting to happen</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;â€œYouâ€™re going to owe me a drink,â€ Catra says. Her movements are awkward as she repositions the baby â€” but sheâ€™s so &lt;i&gt;gentle&lt;/i&gt;. She has retracted her claws, but she still gingerly cups the back of the babyâ€™s head as if scared she might somehow harm him. â€œWhere did you even get this?â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adora takes another drink. â€œThe mom just, like, handed him to me and ran off.â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œWeird,â€ Catra says, and then â€” as if on instinct â€” she starts doing this weird bouncing thing, the babyâ€™s soft, peach-fuzz still head cupped in her hand. â€œWho does that?â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adora nods, agreeing vehemently. â€œRight?â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œIf I had a baby I wouldnâ€™t just hand it to some stranger,â€ says Catra with a roll of her eyes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It's such a simple sentiment, yet it makes Adora's world spin.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;center&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;______________&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/center&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adora and Catra with children through the years, or: Five times kids liked She-Ra more than Adora (and one time one didnâ€™t).&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
